 "help": "usage: wgsextract ref index [-h] [--download | --no-download] [--aligner {bwa,bwa-mem2}]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --download, --no-download\n                        Allow missing public reference/model downloads; no sample files or\n                        genotypes are uploaded. Hosts and request data: docs/privacy.md. Default:\n                        config allow_reference_downloads, else off.\n  --aligner {bwa,bwa-mem2}\n                        Aligner index to make. bwa-mem2's maps faster but takes 17 GB of memory\n                        for a human genome; --download permits fetching hs38DH's, others need ~90\n                        GB of memory to build.\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract ref index --ref hs38.fa\n  wgsextract ref index --ref hs38.fa --aligner bwa-mem2\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  Beside the FASTA: .fai, .dict and the aligner's index files.\n\nneeds:\n  samtools; depending on options and inputs, also: bwa, bwa-mem2, curl; hours,\n  once per reference.\n",
